{
  "id": "COMPOUND:3624 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "Cadaverine is linked to Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 through a series of intermediate targets, primarily Potassium channel subfamily K member 3. This protein acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 2-Hydroxyquinoline and Khonklonginol F, which are themselves linked to the same target. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Potassium channel subfamily K member 3 suggests a potential mechanism where Cadaverine may influence the activity of this protein, thereby affecting the function of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. The evidence supports a role for Cadaverine in modulating the expression or activity of Potassium channel subfamily K member 3, which in turn may interact with Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Potassium channel subfamily K member 3 as a central mediator in the relationship between Cadaverine and Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1.",
